    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, CURRENT] 2026-11-01 review on dev 100b6fbb6e: fixture a.ts with relative imports of missing ./local and ./types reproduces both shapes: FromLocal -extends-> typescript:external:0-0:Local:external_symbol and class C -extends-> ...:Unextracted:external_symbol (origin inheritance-linker). js_ts.py:3422 still drops these; _external_base_edge (inheritance.py:327) has no relative-import check. The class case, previously unmeasured, is now confirmed. (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\nSurfaced by WI-kalug-takiz-lumim-falaj-kopuf-tapor-kizof-sajur (2026-09-30).\n\nThe js_ts analyzer and the core inheritance linker disagree on a base imported from a RELATIVE path that resolves to no symbol. js_ts `_extract_inheritance_edges` deliberately DROPS it (\"A base imported from a RELATIVE path is intra-repo ... drop it rather than mislabel it as external\"; pinned by test_relative_import_unresolved_base_not_mislabeled_external, which calls the ANALYZER only). The core linker's WI-jubag Approach-C fallback (`_external_base_edge`, linkers/inheritance.py) then mints exactly that mislabel, because the source has no analyzer unresolved edge (so `src_has_analyzer_external` is False) and the name is not an in-tree symbol name.\n\nREPRO (measured, interface source, on the WI-kalug branch): a.ts = `import { Local } from \"./local\";` + `export interface FromLocal extends Local {}` with no ./local file -> survey emits FromLocal -extends-> typescript:external:0-0:Local:external_symbol, origin inheritance-linker.\nNOT measured: the class source (`class C extends Unextracted` from './types'); it goes through the same code path in both layers, but no survey was run for it.\n\nThe analyzer's decision is not visible to the linker (it is an absence). Cure shape is a positive record of \"dropped as intra-repo\" the linker can read, or a relative-import check in the linker; ABSENT != EMPTY."  # 850b
